A||N||4||Calab52||Custimizing Torsion rods???||||1||
Z||000000||Calab52||09-26-2001||10:32 PM||||Does anybody know if you can bend the torsion rods to make them fit properly? I was thinking of using a blow torch to adjust the angle of the rod. Thanks in Advance!||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||09-26-2001||11:22 PM||||GAGK!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> No! you can't heat them. Springs are an exact science. You heat them You ruin them. You cannot regain the correct tempering with a torch...<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||4
Z||000002||fierohoho||09-26-2001||11:43 PM||||Ogre is correct but you can have it done if you follow my instructions.<P>The only way to do this would be to find a heat treat shop and start by having them find out how "hard" the bar is and record it for you.<P>I would recomend bringing in another bar for them to test and tell them it's OK to cut that one up to do their testing.<P>Spring temper is usually around 48 to 54 Rockwell which is the hardness, the torsion bars should be close to that.<P>Next thing is to have them anneal the torsion bar and the sample piece which removes the hardness.<P>Next take the bar home and do your custom bending.<P>When you get the bar bent where you like it take it back to the heat treat shop and have them re-harden it to the test specs along with the sample piece so they can test the hardness without damaging the good bar.<P>If you go this route ask them to try and minimize any distortion during the heat treating process, but don't be supprised if you get a little.<P>I did this type of work for 7 years and while it can't be done at home you can have it done.<P>If you go this route post the hardness they find for me, it may come in handy in the future. HoHo <P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pennockpic.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by fierohoho (edited 09-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||09-27-2001||03:20 AM||||For the decklid?  Just get rodney's replacement strut.  It's cooler anyway.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Calab52:<BR><B>Does anybody know if you can bend the torsion rods to make them fit properly? I was thinking of using a blow torch to adjust the angle of the rod. Thanks in Advance!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
